pi-lsp

Selected LSP lifecycle, stdio JSON-RPC transport, and built-in server discovery
conventions are adapted from pi-lsp-client source commit
9d029fb32b721c038b58fb418b98bbfcf720cf0a (MIT):
https://github.com/code-yeongyu/pi-lsp-client
This extension is an independent, narrower implementation; it does not include
the upstream UI, installer, mutation tools, project config loader, directory
scanning, or post-edit diagnostics features.

The upstream pi-lsp-client notice is retained here:

pi-lsp-client

This package is a port of the LSP (Language Server Protocol) tool stack from
oh-my-openagent (omo) at https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent
(originally licensed under the Sustainable Use License 1.0).

The original author Yeongyu Kim (https://github.com/code-yeongyu) has
re-licensed the ported source under MIT for distribution as a pi-coding-agent
extension. See LICENSE for the MIT terms.

The vscode-jsonrpc transport library is by Microsoft
(https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node). Distributed under
the MIT License.

The pi-coding-agent host is by Mario Zechner
(https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono). Distributed under the MIT License.
